    "function": "Catalyzes the hydrolytic removal of ribose 5'-monophosphate from nitrogen N6-modified adenosines, the final step of bioactive cytokinin synthesis. Is involved in the synthesis of isopentenyladenine (iP) and 2-methylthio-iP (2MeS-iP), the most abundant cytokinins detected in M.tuberculosis lysates and supernatants. Is also able to convert trans-zeatin-riboside monophosphate (tZRMP) to trans-zeatin (tZ) in vitro; however, it may not be involved in the biosynthesis of this minor cytokinin in vivo. Accumulation of Rv1205 sensitizes M.tuberculosis to nitric oxide since cytokinin breakdown products ",
